### Enhancements

* Introduce `NoticeBus` (class-level broadcast bus) for channel and plugin notices. Channel notices are broadcast as a side effect of `RepodataFetch` fetching repodata, so they fire regardless of solver backend (classic or `conda-libmamba-solver`, which bypasses `SubdirData.load()`). All CLI subcommands are wrapped in `do_call()` with the notices pub/sub lifecycle. Plugin notices are not subject to the channel-notice fetch interval. (#14157)

### Deprecations

* Mark `conda.notices.core.retrieve_notices` as pending deprecation, to be removed in 27.9. Use `broadcast_channel_notices()`, `broadcast_plugin_notices()`, and `NoticeBus` directly. (#14157)
* Mark `conda.notices.core.display_notices` as pending deprecation, to be removed in 27.9. Use `show_notices()` with notices from `NoticeBus.consume()` instead. (#14157)
* Mark `conda.notices.types.ChannelNoticeResultSet` as pending deprecation, to be removed in 27.9. Use `NoticeBus` and `show_notices()` instead. (#14157)
* Mark `conda.notices.core.notices` as pending deprecation, to be removed in 27.9. `do_call()` wraps all CLI subcommands in `run_notices_sandwich()`; the decorator is a no-op. (#14157)
